==Overview==
<tabber>
Pros=
{{Overview|Pros
|'''General'''
* Good for combo extending and stunning enemies.
* Great damage.
* Amazing mobility.
* Both moves stun the enemy in place.

|'''[Z] Dough Hurricane'''
* Can still drill the enemy even if the enemy uses another skill, similar to the mechanics of [[Dough]].
* Long stun.
* Great mobility.

|'''[X] Flying Trident Pull'''
* Great range.
* Great combo extender, as it can pull the enemy back into a combo.
* Can pull the user to a certain location, making it relatively decent for mobility.
}}

|-|Cons=
{{Overview|Cons
|'''General'''
* Can be hard to PvP with due to the moves needing perfect aim to land on the enemy. The player will usually need a stun move to start a combo with this sword.
* Cannot hit [[Blade]] users.
* Does not [[Instinct Break]], making it really easy to dodge.
* Both moves are single targets.
* Small hitbox makes it hard to aim with.
* Slow M1 speed.

|'''[Z] Dough Hurricane'''
* Enemies can ken-trick and [[Flash Step]] instantly near the user after the knockback, leaving them vulnerable. (This can happen when PvP on ground with good [[instinct]] players)
* Cannot be canceled upon hitting an enemy.
** The user can drown while dragging an enemy into the [[water]] or [[lava]].
* High delay if missed.

|'''[X] Flying Trident Pull'''
* Require good aim.
** Missing can cause the user to rush close to the enemy if they are in the wall or on the ground, leaving them vulnerable to counterattacks because of the slight delay after getting pulled.
}}
</tabber>

==Trivia==
* As of [[Updates/20|Update 20]], while using transformed [[Buddha]], {{Ability|Z}} moves the user a very short distance. {{Ability|X}} is harder to hit with transformed [[Buddha]] since it will aim parallel to the ground if aimed downward while standing on the ground.
* The player can perform a glitch by coordinating with another player to use {{Ability|Z}} and aim it downward, which results in both users being knocked back a great distance if done correctly.
* Interestingly, each sea features a sword named "Trident": the [[Trident]] in [[First Sea]], the [[Dragon Trident]] in [[Second Sea]], and the Spikey Trident in [[Third Sea]].
*Aiming {{Ability|X}} at the back wall of the [[Mansion]] in [[Third Sea]] allows you to noclip through the wall to the windmill outside.

